# Files that ship into the Linux container must be LF on every platform.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows plus deploy/azure-deploy.ps1, which hands
# `az acr build` the LOCAL working tree as the build context, means a fresh
# Windows clone would otherwise ship CRLF copies. The failure modes are not
# symmetric: a CRLF shell script fails loudly (dash chokes and the container
# will not boot), but a CRLF /etc/cron.d entry corrupts its trailing field and
# cron reports that only through syslog/mail — both no-ops in this image. The
# container boots, uvicorn serves, CI is green, and the schedule simply never
# fires.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the files that ship: no repo-wide `* text=auto`, which
# would renormalize unrelated files.
deploy/crontab text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
